  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Thursday)\nIssued at 1222 PM CDT FRI OCT 23 2026\n\nHigh pressure will remain the dominant feature through the middle\nof the week, with very little change anticipated in the forecast,\nor impacts for central Alabama. Dry conditions are expected to\ncontinue, with no rain in the forecast for the next seven days.\nTemperatures will also remain relatively stable under the ridge,\nwith highs ranging in the mid to upper-70s, and lows ranging in\nthe 40s. The exception to this will be Monday night, when the\napex of the ridge will slightly shift east. This will allow for\ncooler air to push farther south under the CAD wedge, with lows\nin the east dropping into the upper-30s.\n\nBy Thursday, the ridge will begin to break down as a trough and\ncold front begin to work through the Midwest. Afternoon highs\nahead of this trough will climb once more, as the region gets put\ninto SW flow aloft, with highs into the weekend ranging in the\nupper-70s to low-80s.\n\n/44/",
